{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0185bzYk4gy5ytMGUmXKLXdY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"c57716bd1b210b880f9ad7b096569454b3783048","date":"2026-09-21T18:21:18+03:00","message":"(chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app (#372)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Share SWR through module federation in the reports app\n\nAdd swr to the reports app's peerDependencies so the build tooling\nfederates it, and pin the exact 2.5.1 dependency the way the other\npackages in this repo do so the fallback copy matches the app shell.\n\nThe openmrs rspack config derives the module federation shared list\nfrom peerDependencies. swr was only reaching the reports app\ntransitively, so the built entry registered no swr share and bundled a\nprivate copy. useSWR from that copy reads its own SWRConfig context,\nnot the one the framework's component decorator provides, so the\nreports app ran with SWR's stock defaults (revalidate on focus and\nreconnect, unlimited retries on every error) and its own cache instead\nof the shared one. The other four packages here already declare the\npeer.\n\nWith the peer declared, the built entry registers swr, swr/_internal,\nswr/immutable and swr/infinite at 2.5.1, matching the other O3 apps.\n\n* Invalidate report lists through the SWR config's mutate\n\nThe cancel modal refreshed the report tables with the global mutate\nimported from swr. That function is bound to SWR's default cache, while\nevery hook rendered under the framework's component decorator lives in\nthe decorator's provider cache, so once swr is federated the global\nmutate no longer reaches those hooks and the tables would not refresh\nafter a cancel or delete. Take mutate from useSWRConfig instead, which\nis bound to the provider cache, and wrap the helper in useCallback so\nthe submit handler's dependency list stays honest.\n\n---------","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d631bae67f92ce1625be3b2c70020b410d101c63","date":"2026-02-10T11:05:41-05:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"cb823c54259513f9b1bbd61225f89708de9312c7","date":"2025-10-20T21:22:02+03:00","message":"(fix) Expand webservices.rest dependency range to support 3.x","refs":"","body":"Updates webservices.rest backend dependency version constraint from ^2.2.0 (or ^2.24.0) to \">=2.2.0\" to support both 2.x stable releases and 3.x pre-release/stable versions. This resolves version compatibility issues when running with webservices.rest 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT.0.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"9795d776cd61b56114d4da597e9b0be1abbe5ff5","date":"2025-06-03T13:37:50-04:00","message":"(fix) Fix the auto-update script and update to the latest version of core (#99)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5954a3acbe9d4799e7cca4455195aeeac6b8f646","date":"2025-05-01T08:23:45-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#78)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9ccfccbef265e6ac29613daf4f67079f28f3375d","date":"2025-04-29T17:53:44+03:00","message":"(fix) Use correct path for fetching ran reports and switch to OpenMRS datepicker(#72)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Emmanuel Nyachoke","authorEmail":"achachiez@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b1a8bac3319eec695f08abb8c85bc3eca8739ddc","date":"2025-02-12T20:53:50+01:00","message":"(chore) O3-1494: Update reporting backend dependencies (#58)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"druchniewicz","authorEmail":"51370022+druchniewicz@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"626b777d3894b352df757af94422b6f8a3852a19","date":"2025-02-06T12:31:06+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-1494: Add report admin dashboard (#45)","refs":"","body":"* O3-1494: Added Report Adm