{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WWNK67SSifBBsHAdKqWAV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools","number":423,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack","state":"merged","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:43.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-10-07T18:48:51.000Z","closedAt":"2026-10-07T18:48:51.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/pull/423","mergeCommit":"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","syncedAt":"2026-10-23T18:59:44.740Z","tickets":[],"commits":[{"sha":"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.component.tsx","additions":14,"deletions":17},{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss","additions":1,"deletions":16},{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/report-parameter-input.component.tsx","additions":1,"deletions":3},{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/run-report/run-report-form.component.tsx","additions":3,"deletions":9},{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/run-report/run-report-form.scss","additions":1,"deletions":20},{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"body":"## Requirements\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\r\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\r\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now wrap their fields in a Carbon `Stack` with `gap={5}`, and the form sets the 16px padding around it. That's the same pattern the OCL subscription form and many of the patient chart form workspaces use.\r\n\r\nBefore, each field set its own spacing. The selects had a fixed `height: 30px` with a 30px bottom margin, the output format select added another 50px margin and 32px of top padding, and each report parameter and the cron editor had their own 16px padding. So the gaps between fields were uneven, and in the edit scheduled report form they stacked on top of the existing `gap={8}`.\r\n\r\nI've also dropped the fixed 300px width on the Report and Output format selects, so they're full width like the parameter inputs.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\n| Before | After |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| <img width=\"350\" alt=\"run-report-before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c493434-7659-419b-889c-4138256b6b80\" /> | <img width=\"350\" alt=\"run-report-after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a229081b-2877-4ced-b3dc-613ad36a0e11\" /> |\r\n| <img width=\"350\" alt=\"edit-scheduled-report-before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/43377201-b4dc-45d1-bdeb-3b58f397a6bc\" /> | <img width=\"350\" alt=\"edit-scheduled-report-after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9c068e7d-1f27-4449-9b6d-959627f45b6d\" /> |\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\n\r\n## Other","comments":[{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:50:44.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=75389876\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\n\n**[Low risk]** Refactors form layout spacing using a design system component\\.\n\nThe PR is not ready to merge until the scheduled-report form keeps its fields from overlapping.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Schedule fields can overlap** <a href=\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/pull/423#discussion_r4192363541\">▶</a>\n\n<details open><summary>Summary</summary>\n\nThe run-report and scheduled-report forms now use a shared Carbon `Stack` to space their fields evenly. The selects no longer have a fixed width, and each form keeps its padding around the shared fields.\n\n- The run-report form spaces its fields evenly.\n- The scheduled-report form spaces its fields evenly.\n</details>\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:4 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"(fix) Space the report form fields evenl...\"](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commit/97649995117f67c9796f7b9edc225f9a88fea899)</sub>"},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:50:47.000Z","state":null,"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.component.tsx","line":336,"body":"<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Schedule fields can overlap**\n\nWhen an administrator edits a scheduled report, the new plain `<div>` around `SimpleCronEditor` has no height because its fields float. The form can place the next parameter or output-format select in the same space. Give the editor a wrapper that contains its floated fields.\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!"},{"kind":"review","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:50:49.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:53:31.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"<!-- greptile_trex_summary -->\n\n<!-- greptile_trex_run:48486 -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=75389876\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a><a href=\"https://www.greptile.com/trex\"><img alt=\"TREX\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/trex/trex_standalone.svg?v=1\" height=\"24\" align=\"top\"></a> TREX</h2>\n\nNo flows tested, and faced 2 obstacles.\n\n### Obstacles faced\n\n- The Reports dev server does not accept connections\\; fix it so the OpenMRS page loads\\.\n- The reporting services are unavailable\\; start them and provide report and schedule data\\.\n\n<sub>To reduce obstacles, [configure your TREX environment](https://app.greptile.com/openmrs/-/trex/5456bb18-a289-48fb-892a-1301373c2220/setup?utm_source=trex_scm_comment).</sub>"},{"kind":"review","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:58:36.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:58:36.000Z","state":null,"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.component.tsx","line":336,"body":"In this form the editor sits in Carbon's `Stack`, which is `display: grid`, so the wrapper already contains its floats (61px tall, next field 16px below). It would collapse outside a grid or flex parent though, so I've given it `display: flow-root`."},{"kind":"review","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:59:09.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-10-06T06:59:09.000Z","state":null,"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.component.tsx","line":336,"body":"You're right — with `SimpleCronEditor` as a child of Carbon's `Stack`, the wrapper contains the floated fields, so the following field won't overlap. Adding `display: flow-root` also makes that containment explicit and keeps the component safe if it's later rendered outside such a formatting context. This resolves my concern; no change is needed."},{"kind":"review","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-10-07T12:37:36.000Z","state":"APPROVED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"github-actions","createdAt":"2026-10-07T13:49:18.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"**Size Change:** 0 B \n\n**Total Size:** 2.63 MB\n\n\n\n<details><summary>ℹ️ <strong>View Unchanged</strong></summary>\n\n| Filename | Size | Change |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/282.js` | 1.1 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/434.js` | 1.1 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/466.js` | 2.58 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/556.js` | 1.1 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/689.js` | 42.5 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/871.js` | 186 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/903.js` | 1.1 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/997.js` | 1.1 kB | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/1442.js` | 267 B | 0 B |\n| `packages/esm-admin-openconceptlab-app/dist/1480.js` 