{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mwdgL6AeSdVLbwEjtuJrq","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"e497c33d0dc9799605b6ab663ddb54f967d8a682","date":"2026-10-02T22:50:33+03:00","message":"(fix) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports (#408)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports\n\nReplaces the bare \"Reports\" heading on the overview page with\nPageHeader and PageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new\nReportsPictogram. The header runs full width under the navbar, with the\nimplementation name above the title like other O3 apps, a white\nbackground, a bottom border, and 16px of space before the action\nbuttons.\n\nThe root container's 32px padding moves onto each page's content so\nthe header can sit flush. The overview no longer passes the\nbreadcrumb slot's negative top margin, which only offset that padding\nand would otherwise pull the header under the navbar. The scheduled\nreports and Reports Webview pages keep the same padding through a page\nwrapper, so their layout doesn't change.\n\nReportsPictogram ships in a framework release after\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\ntypechecks.\n\n* Mock the page header in the overview tests\n\nThe overview tests mock @openmrs/esm-framework with a factory that only\nlists the exports they use. The overview now renders PageHeader,\nPageHeaderContent and ReportsPictogram, so add simple mocks for them.\n\n* Assert that the Reports overview renders its page header\n\nThe overview test mocked PageHeader, PageHeaderContent and\nReportsPictogram but never checked them, so it would still pass if the\nheader or pictogram were removed. It now checks for the \"Reports\"\nheading and the pictogram.\n\n* Drop the breadcrumbs slot from the Reports overview\n\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more. No extension attaches to\nit, and the app shell no longer mounts its breadcrumbs component. The\noverview's slot had no class, so it rendered as an empty element and\nremoving it doesn't change the layout. The test mock for ExtensionSlot\ngoes with it.\n\n* Rename tests to drop the .component suffix\n\nTest files don't carry the component-kind suffix. Rename the three that\ndid in admin-tools:\n\n- reports-app overview.component.test.tsx -> overview.test.tsx\n- reports-app reports-data-overview.component.test.tsx -> reports-data-overview.test.tsx\n- metadataexport-app view-package-action-button.component.test.tsx -> view-package-action-button.test.tsx\n\nThe only content change is the trailing newline Prettier adds to\nreports-data-overview.test.tsx.\n\n* Remove breadcrumbs from the Reports app\n\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more, so the Reports pages\nwere rendering empty slots and registering breadcrumbs nobody reads.\n\n- Remove the breadcrumbs slot from the Scheduled reports and Reports\n  data overview pages, and the .breadcrumb rule. Its negative top margin\n  cancelled the page's top padding, so .page now drops its top padding\n  instead and the content stays flush under the navbar.\n- Remove the registerBreadcrumbs call from startupApp, along with the\n  getFixedT setup that only it used.\n- Drop the ExtensionSlot mock from the data overview test.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"bf73010a71a9859e4c8938452ac0c7221c891852","date":"2026-10-02T22:32:29+03:00","message":"(feat) Add a page header with the concept dictionary pictogram to OCL (#409)","refs":"","body":"Replaces the bare \"OCL Subscription Module\" heading with PageHeader and\nPageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new ConceptDictionaryPictogram.\nThe header runs full width under the navbar, with the implementation\nname above the title like other O3 apps, a bottom border, and 16px of\nspace before the tabs.\n\nConceptDictionaryPictogram ships in a framework release after\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\ntypechecks and before the root component test can render it from the\nframework mock.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198","date":"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00","message":"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app","refs":"","body":"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\nnone of these are:\n\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\n  only welcome used)\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterElement,\n  cancelActionButton, tableIcon, rowCellEven, rowCellOdd\n- components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss:\n  reportButton\n- components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss: cronEditor\n\nrowCellEven, rowCellOdd and reportButton are still in use, but from\nother stylesheets: the overview tables use the copies in reports.scss,\nand the run report form uses the copy in run-report-form.scss. Only the\nunreferenced duplicates are removed.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"83ac02f0cb2cd7404a92939eb9718280b01e4a94","date":"2026-09-04T13:20:14+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5920: Implement View Package functionality (#337)","refs":"","body":"* update error handling in package creation workspace\n\n* add status column and action button column\n\n* add view package util\n\n* make exportPackage parameter is required\n\n* add usePackageBuilds hook to fetch package builds\n\n* add ViewPackageActionButton component and tests\n\n* add view package workspace\n\n* add translations\n\n* config routes\n\n* add testing for view package workspace\n\n* update tests\n\n* simplify action button rendering in PackagesTable component\n\n* reorder import in PackagesTable component\n\n* capitalization in package status messages\n\n* correct import path for types in packages.resource.ts\n\n* use formatDuration() instread dayjs's RelativeTime\n\n* fix speling mistake view package util\n\n* fix typo in mock import path for view-package-utils\n\n* refacto find packages by uuid\n\n* Remove unnecessary mock clearing in ViewPackageActionButton tests and rename view package utility file\n\n* Fix import order in ViewPackageWorkspace test file\n\n* import statement formatting in packages.resource.ts\n\n* Add translation comments\n\n* update translation file\n\n* add tests to verify build status rendering and view workspace functionality\n\n* update access privilege checks from 'Manage Metadata Export Packages' to 'Get Metadata Export Packages'\n\n* update import order\n\n* removing unnecessary parameters\n\n* remove unused styles\n\n* add test to verify loading state f\n\n* add tranlation key\n\n* add error message display for failed builds\n\n* add access control for package downloads\n\n* fix typo\n\n* remove space\n\n* update download link to use dynamic URL based on build UUID\n\n* update tests\n\n* fix minior formatting issue\n\n* remove duplicate assertion\n\n* update build timestamps in test to reflect realistic timing","authorName":"Bawantha Thilan","authorEmail":"38850236+Bawanthathilan@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"16972a9625452dceb98318d3b59d8e49eb68e935","date":"2026-07-31T01:55:13+03:00","message":"(fix) Remove nested anchors from the Legacy Admin and OCL admin cards","refs":"","body":"Both cards wrapped ClickableTile in an outer anchor. ClickableTile\nrenders its own anchor, so this produced invalid nested anchors and a\ndead tab stop: keyboard users would focus the outer link, then land on\nthe tile itself, which had tabindex 0 but no href and did nothing on\nEnter.\n\nThe Legacy Admin card now passes href, target, and rel directly to\nClickableTile, keeping its new tab behavior. Carbon's ClickableTileProps\ntype omits target even though the component forwards extra props to the\nunderlying anchor, so those props are passed via a spread.\n\nThe OCL card keeps its client-side same-tab navigation by calling\nnavigate from an onClick handler for plain left clicks, mirroring what\nConfigurableLink does. Modified clicks fall through to the anchor and\nstill open a new tab or window.\n\nThe cardLink wrapper styles are no longer needed since there is no\nouter anchor left to reset.\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"2328ed70a6917302a0bc32d47a9873598363442c","date":"2023-06-14T15:41:15-04:00","message":"(fix) Adjust System Admin page styles for responsiveness (#24)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":6}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255947d-acba-483f-a10d-51666b0220d5","uuid":"b4d893ef-7bd0-4b77-9f33-d8b9923f1154","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:18:59.691Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"e497c33d0dc9799605b6ab663ddb54f967d8a682","date":"2026-10-02T22:50:33+03:00","message":"(fix) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports (#408)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Add a page header with the reports pictogram to Reports\n\nReplaces the bare \"Reports\" heading on the overview page with\nPageHeader and PageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new\nReportsPictogram. The header runs full width under the navbar, with the\nimplementation name above the title like other O3 apps, a white\nbackground, a bottom border, and 16px of space before the action\nbuttons.\n\nThe root container's 32px padding moves onto each page's content so\nthe header can sit flush. The overview no longer passes the\nbreadcrumb slot's negative top margin, which only offset that padding\nand would otherwise pull the header under the navbar. The scheduled\nreports and Reports Webview pages keep the same padding through a page\nwrapper, so their layout doesn't change.\n\nReportsPictogram ships in a framework release after\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\ntypechecks.\n\n* Mock the page header in the overview tests\n\nThe overview tests mock @openmrs/esm-framework with a factory that only\nlists the exports they use. The overview now renders PageHeader,\nPageHeaderContent and ReportsPictogram, so add simple mocks for them.\n\n* Assert that the Reports overview renders its page header\n\nThe overview test mocked PageHeader, PageHeaderContent and\nReportsPictogram but never checked them, so it would still pass if the\nheader or pictogram were removed. It now checks for the \"Reports\"\nheading and the pictogram.\n\n* Drop the breadcrumbs slot from the Reports overview\n\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more. No extension attaches to\nit, and the app shell no longer mounts its breadcrumbs component. The\noverview's slot had no class, so it rendered as an empty element and\nremoving it doesn't change the layout. The test mock for ExtensionSlot\ngoes with it.\n\n* Rename tests to drop the .component suffix\n\nTest files don't carry the component-kind suffix. Rename the three that\ndid in admin-tools:\n\n- reports-app overview.component.test.tsx -> overview.test.tsx\n- reports-app reports-data-overview.component.test.tsx -> reports-data-overview.test.tsx\n- metadataexport-app view-package-action-button.component.test.tsx -> view-package-action-button.test.tsx\n\nThe only content change is the trailing newline Prettier adds to\nreports-data-overview.test.tsx.\n\n* Remove breadcrumbs from the Reports app\n\nNothing renders into breadcrumbs-slot any more, so the Reports pages\nwere rendering empty slots and registering breadcrumbs nobody reads.\n\n- Remove the breadcrumbs slot from the Scheduled reports and Reports\n  data overview pages, and the .breadcrumb rule. Its negative top margin\n  cancelled the page's top padding, so .page now drops its top padding\n  instead and the content stays flush under the navbar.\n- Remove the registerBreadcrumbs call from startupApp, along with the\n  getFixedT setup that only it used.\n- Drop the ExtensionSlot mock from the data overview test.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"bf73010a71a9859e4c8938452ac0c7221c891852","date":"2026-10-02T22:32:29+03:00","message":"(feat) Add a page header with the concept dictionary pictogram to OCL (#409)","refs":"","body":"Replaces the bare \"OCL Subscription Module\" heading with PageHeader and\nPageHeaderContent, using the styleguide's new ConceptDictionaryPictogram.\nThe header runs full width under the navbar, with the implementation\nname above the title like other O3 apps, a bottom border, and 16px of\nspace before the tabs.\n\nConceptDictionaryPictogram ships in a framework release after\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core adds it, so this needs that release before it\ntypechecks and before the root component test can render it from the\nframework mock.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198","date":"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00","message":"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app","refs":"","body":"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\nnone of these are:\n\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\n  only welcome used)\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterE