{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4uyKCDfsNdzGZe3TyBzaL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools","number":358,"kind":"pr","title":"(chore) O3-5965: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from reports app","state":"merged","author":"solomonfortune","createdAt":"2026-09-13T09:11:56.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-10-01T18:08:14.000Z","closedAt":"2026-10-01T18:08:14.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/pull/358","mergeCommit":"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac","syncedAt":"2026-10-23T18:59:44.740Z","tickets":[{"key":"O3-5965","source":"ticket-pattern"}],"commits":[{"sha":"fbda030326a3a0a691844ad052fe7aed34ca44ac","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports.scss","additions":0,"deletions":16}],"body":"## Requirements\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\r\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\r\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nRemoves four `width: 100%` rules in `reports.scss` targeting `.cds--date-picker`, `.cds--select`, `.cds--select-input`, and `.cds--date-picker__input`. These selectors lack `:global()`, so CSS Modules rewrites their class names and they never match Carbon's actual markup — the rules have never had any effect. This is a behavior-preserving dead code removal.\r\n\r\nVerified via:\r\n- Grep confirms no `cds--` class names remain in the file\r\n- Production build passes\r\n- Existing test and lint suites pass unchanged\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\nNot applicable — no visual or behavioral change, since the removed rules were already inert.\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\nhttps://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3-5965\r\n\r\n## Other\r\nNo new tests added intentionally: the deleted rules had no effect, so there is no new behavior to cover. A clean production build is the verification that no rendering depended on them.","comments":[{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-09-13T09:19:09.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=63585264\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=1\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=1\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=1\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\nSafe to merge; the reports filter controls maintain their intended container-width layout after the stylesheet cleanup.\n\nWhat we checked:\n- T-Rex executed the width-check script against the updated stylesheet to validate desktop and mobile widths for the report filter controls. <a href=\"https://www.greptile.com/trex\"><img alt=\"T-Rex\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/trex/trex_green.svg\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\"></a>\n- T-Rex captured and organized before/after videos and screenshots, along with a dedicated width-check artifact, to document the observed layout changes. <a href=\"https://www.greptile.com/trex\"><img alt=\"T-Rex\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/trex/trex_green.svg\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\"></a>\n- T-Rex ran a follow-up validation comparing base and HEAD renderings at 1024px and 390px to verify the width results. <a href=\"h